1
00:01:51,837 --> 00:01:53,697
Hanging around here won't do any good.

2
00:01:54,077 --> 00:01:55,617
Let's head back to the ship for now.

3
00:01:55,817 --> 00:01:57,677
We left Nami there all by ourself.

4
00:01:58,237 --> 00:01:59,577
And Robin's still missing.

5
00:02:00,717 --> 00:02:02,397
The ship's a problem, too.

6
00:02:03,237 --> 00:02:03,557
Yeah.

7
00:02:04,117 --> 00:02:04,977
Hey, Luffy!

8
00:02:08,137 --> 00:02:09,497
I've made a decision.

9
00:02:10,497 --> 00:02:11,617
About the ship.

10
00:02:14,177 --> 00:02:16,597
It's time to part ways with the Mary.

11
00:02:17,317 --> 00:02:18,937
We'll say goodbye to her here.

12
00:02:21,077 --> 00:02:28,457
Big fight under the moon.

13
00:02:28,677 --> 00:02:30,917
The pirate flag flutters with sorrow.

14
00:02:35,837 --> 00:02:36,557
Hey!

15
00:02:37,357 --> 00:02:39,277
Usopp's finally awake, you guys!

16
00:02:39,457 --> 00:02:40,157
All right!

17
00:02:40,297 --> 00:02:41,177
Good to hear!

18
00:02:42,797 --> 00:02:44,757
That's one less thing to worry about.

19
00:02:48,317 --> 00:02:49,557
Hey, Usopp!

20
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:56,877
Robin still isn't back yet.

21
00:02:58,717 --> 00:03:02,277
You know, I ought to punch you for scaring us like that.

22
00:03:03,577 --> 00:03:04,797
Yeah, no kidding.

23
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:08,157
Though it looks like you've taken enough punches already, if you ask me.

24
00:03:08,417 --> 00:03:10,957
What were you thinking, taking those guys on alone?

25
00:03:10,957 --> 00:03:13,937
You can't just run off and fight whoever you want.

26
00:03:14,117 --> 00:03:16,317
Oh, that's a good one coming from you.

27
00:03:18,057 --> 00:03:20,717
This wouldn't have happened if I was strong like you guys.

28
00:03:20,917 --> 00:03:21,837
I'm sorry!

29
00:03:21,837 --> 00:03:24,097
It's all my fault!

30
00:03:24,557 --> 00:03:26,437
I'm so ashamed of myself!

31
00:03:30,437 --> 00:03:32,397
I knew how important that money was to us!

32
00:03:32,397 --> 00:03:33,137
Hey, hey, stop!

33
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:34,197
I get it!

34
00:03:34,457 --> 00:03:37,657
I know you're sorry, but you don't have to get all touchy-feely on me, okay?

35
00:03:37,657 --> 00:03:38,817
With all our savings!

36
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,577
All the trouble we went through!

37
00:03:40,797 --> 00:03:41,957
What about the Mary?

38
00:03:42,337 --> 00:03:42,977
Take it easy!

39
00:03:43,237 --> 00:03:44,817
You shouldn't be out of bed yet!

40
00:03:44,817 --> 00:03:46,157
Come on, calm down!

41
00:03:46,397 --> 00:03:48,417
Stop your whining and listen to the doctor!

42
00:03:50,357 --> 00:03:55,117
So, is there a chance we might get our money back after all?

43
00:03:55,737 --> 00:03:56,877
Well, maybe.

44
00:03:57,177 --> 00:03:59,677
We won't know for sure till that Frankie guy shows up.

45
00:04:00,557 --> 00:04:01,277
I see.

46
00:04:01,677 --> 00:04:02,537
I'm sorry.

47
00:04:03,617 --> 00:04:04,097
Hey!

48
00:04:04,317 --> 00:04:07,937
Even if we can't get the rest back, we still have a hundred million berries left over!

49
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:08,917
Don't worry!

50
00:04:11,917 --> 00:04:13,977
Yeah, but he lost twice that much!

51
00:04:14,817 --> 00:04:15,217
Nami!

52
00:04:16,557 --> 00:04:17,597
Sorry, Yusup.

53
00:04:18,077 --> 00:04:18,397
No.

54
00:04:18,977 --> 00:04:19,757
It's fine.

55
00:04:20,337 --> 00:04:24,017
More importantly, is Mary gonna be okay?

56
00:04:25,457 --> 00:04:28,597
I mean, can we get her repaired with the money that we have left?

57
00:04:29,297 --> 00:04:32,077
We're lucky we have all these awesome shipwrights to work on her.

58
00:04:32,337 --> 00:04:36,577
But I know things are gonna get rough out there, so I want her to be stronger than ever before!

59
00:04:37,317 --> 00:04:39,657
We gotta do a lot more than just a little touch-up.

60
00:04:39,657 --> 00:04:44,697
So, do you think those guys will still do a good job if we only have a hundred million to pay with?

61
00:04:44,817 --> 00:04:46,317
You talked to them about it, right?

62
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:47,617
Uh, yeah.

63
00:04:47,997 --> 00:04:49,917
But we aren't having them repair it.

64
00:04:50,717 --> 00:04:52,877
We decided to get a new ship instead!

65
00:04:52,877 --> 00:04:59,017
I know that we probably should have asked you first, but we didn't have much choice.

66
00:04:59,417 --> 00:05:00,997
Either way, I've made up my mind.

67
00:05:01,317 --> 00:05:06,117
The Going Mary has taken good care of us, but it looks like our journey with her has to end here.

68
00:05:06,117 --> 00:05:28,797
Anyway, Ice Pops gave us this awesome ship catalog to flip through.

69
00:05:28,797 --> 00:05:31,457
There's all kinds of different ships we could pick from in here.

70
00:05:31,577 --> 00:05:35,237
And if we decided to shop for a used model, we could go bigger than the Mary.

71
00:05:35,517 --> 00:05:37,537
And still keep our budget under a hundred million.

72
00:05:37,697 --> 00:05:38,077
Wait.

73
00:05:39,457 --> 00:05:40,557
Just stop.

74
00:05:40,937 --> 00:05:41,897
I get it, Luffy.

75
00:05:42,197 --> 00:05:44,457
But the joke's gone on long enough, okay?

76
00:05:44,897 --> 00:05:45,337
See?

77
00:05:46,017 --> 00:05:47,297
Chopper doesn't know you're kidding.

78
00:05:47,857 --> 00:05:49,437
Look how upset this is making him.

79
00:05:50,137 --> 00:05:51,017
Jeez, Captain.

80
00:05:51,237 --> 00:05:53,517
You should know better than to treat your crew like that.

81
00:05:53,897 --> 00:05:54,717
Come on, Nami.

82
00:05:54,897 --> 00:05:55,777
Back me up here.

83
00:05:58,797 --> 00:06:01,037
Hold up.

84
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:04,857
Does that mean we don't have enough for the repairs?

85
00:06:05,257 --> 00:06:07,777
It's because I lost the 200 million, isn't it?

86
00:06:07,997 --> 00:06:09,957
And now we can't afford the work on the Mary.

87
00:06:10,137 --> 00:06:11,237
Is that what this is about?

88
00:06:11,837 --> 00:06:14,877
After all, a first-class shipyard is going to cost a lot, right?

89
00:06:15,037 --> 00:06:16,817
Would you stop and listen to me?

90
00:06:16,997 --> 00:06:17,897
What is it?

91
00:06:18,517 --> 00:06:19,397
Tell me!

92
00:06:19,817 --> 00:06:21,437
Don't try to sugarcoat it!

93
00:06:21,497 --> 00:06:22,417
I'm not, okay?

94
00:06:22,717 --> 00:06:24,537
I don't even care that you lost all the money.

95
00:06:24,617 --> 00:06:25,597
That's over now!

96
00:06:25,597 --> 00:06:28,777
If that's how you feel, then what's with all this crap about buying a new ship?

97
00:06:28,797 --> 00:06:29,777
Both of you, stop it!

98
00:06:29,937 --> 00:06:31,097
Fighting isn't going to help.

99
00:06:31,857 --> 00:06:33,537
Just calm down for a sec.

100
00:06:34,757 --> 00:06:36,417
I don't see what I'm doing wrong.

101
00:06:36,557 --> 00:06:38,357
He's the one saying all this dumb stuff!

102
00:06:38,477 --> 00:06:41,657
I know how you feel, but you shouldn't get so worked up right now.

103
00:06:42,197 --> 00:06:43,557
Listen to Nami, Usopp.

104
00:06:43,617 --> 00:06:45,857
If you don't get any rest, you're not going to get better.

105
00:06:46,297 --> 00:06:47,697
Who cares about me?

106
00:06:47,897 --> 00:06:50,997
How can you just sit here when he's making jokes about getting a new ship?

107
00:06:51,177 --> 00:06:52,717
I'm not joking about anything!

108
00:06:52,877 --> 00:06:54,877
This was a hard decision for me, too!

109
00:06:54,877 --> 00:06:56,997
Oh, yeah, I feel really sorry for you!

110
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,737
Already window shopping for a new toy!

111
00:07:01,417 --> 00:07:03,177
You trying to pick a fight with me?

112
00:07:03,257 --> 00:07:04,957
I don't want your damn pity, got it?

113
00:07:05,237 --> 00:07:07,437
If you tell me it doesn't matter that I lost the money,

114
00:07:07,537 --> 00:07:09,617
then why are you talking about buying a new ship?

115
00:07:10,077 --> 00:07:11,377
Just spit it out already!

116
00:07:11,697 --> 00:07:14,577
If we can't afford the repairs because I screwed up, then tell me!

117
00:07:14,737 --> 00:07:17,257
Don't show me some stupid catalog and change the subject!

118
00:07:17,517 --> 00:07:18,857
I want to know the truth!

119
00:07:18,857 --> 00:07:21,417
The Mary can't be!

120
00:07:33,097 --> 00:07:33,737
What?

121
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,057
What did you just say?

122
00:07:37,437 --> 00:07:39,717
Don't make me repeat myself!

123
00:07:39,977 --> 00:07:42,817
I told you, the Mary can't be repaired anymore!

124
00:07:43,357 --> 00:07:45,857
No matter what we do, we...

125
00:07:45,857 --> 00:07:47,577
We can't fix it!

126
00:07:47,577 --> 00:07:51,197
Otherwise, I wouldn't say something like that!

127
00:07:52,197 --> 00:07:53,737
You mean this ship?

128
00:07:53,817 --> 00:07:56,177
The ship that we're riding on right now is broken?

129
00:07:56,537 --> 00:07:57,277
That's right!

130
00:07:57,857 --> 00:08:00,257
It's only a matter of time before she sinks!

131
00:08:02,737 --> 00:08:04,457
What are you talking about, Luffy?

132
00:08:04,677 --> 00:08:05,537
That's nuts!

133
00:08:05,697 --> 00:08:06,617
No, I'm serious!

134
00:08:07,117 --> 00:08:09,297
The shipwrights took a look at the Mary themselves!

135
00:08:09,297 --> 00:08:13,197
They said she wouldn't even hold out until the next island!

136
00:08:13,717 --> 00:08:15,997
And it's settled, so that's it?

137
00:08:16,517 --> 00:08:20,477
A bunch of strangers tell you to scrap your ship and you don't even ask any questions?

138
00:08:20,797 --> 00:08:21,657
That's enough!

139
00:08:21,657 --> 00:08:26,517
I understand these guys know what they're talking about, but this is just wrong!

140
00:08:27,897 --> 00:08:29,597
Don't give up on the Mary!

141
00:08:30,037 --> 00:08:32,337
What about all the adventures we've gone on together?

142
00:08:32,617 --> 00:08:34,657
What about all the battles we've fought?

143
00:08:34,817 --> 00:08:35,997
She's our friend!

144
00:08:36,317 --> 00:08:37,637
She's one of us!

145
00:08:37,997 --> 00:08:41,877
Are you going to abandon her for another ship without a second thought?

146
00:08:41,877 --> 00:08:49,817
After all we've been through, is that how little the Mary meets to you, Luffy?

147
00:08:53,137 --> 00:08:56,137
I know you're upset, Usopp, but you need to calm down!

148
00:08:56,637 --> 00:08:57,817
Sorry, but no!

149
00:08:59,817 --> 00:09:02,557
I'm not packing down until we settle this!

150
00:09:02,817 --> 00:09:03,837
Usopp, please!

151
00:09:06,577 --> 00:09:07,097
What?

152
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:09,417
So you know better than the shipwrights?

153
00:09:09,417 --> 00:09:15,277
If we had someone on the crew who knew about this stuff, we wouldn't have asked them in the first place!

154
00:09:15,437 --> 00:09:16,557
Then forget them!

155
00:09:16,917 --> 00:09:18,977
We don't need those guys telling us what to do!

156
00:09:19,377 --> 00:09:21,937
I'll repair the Mary myself, just like before!

157
00:09:22,217 --> 00:09:25,617
We've made it this far, so there's no reason we can't go on that way!

158
00:09:25,897 --> 00:09:27,577
Here, I'll get started right now!

159
00:09:27,977 --> 00:09:29,397
Come on, guys, help me out!

160
00:09:29,517 --> 00:09:30,837
That's not gonna work!

161
00:09:31,277 --> 00:09:33,417
That's right, we don't have enough lumber, do we?

162
00:09:33,757 --> 00:09:35,797
I better go buy some at the shipyard!

163
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,777
We've got a lot of work to do!

164
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:39,577
You're not a shipwright, Usopp!

165
00:09:39,657 --> 00:09:40,537
You hear me?!

166
00:09:40,537 --> 00:09:41,497
Stop it, Luffy!

167
00:09:42,437 --> 00:09:43,737
Yeah, you're right, I know!

168
00:09:44,237 --> 00:09:45,137
But so what?

169
00:09:45,317 --> 00:09:48,797
I don't see why you're so hung up on everything those stupid shipwrights say!

170
00:09:49,157 --> 00:09:52,397
If they knew what she'd gone through, they wouldn't give up on the Mary so easy!

171
00:09:52,497 --> 00:09:53,837
They just want your money!

172
00:09:54,237 --> 00:09:54,717
Usopp?

173
00:09:55,277 --> 00:09:59,537
The Mary's our ship, so it's our job to take care of her without someone else butting in!

174
00:10:00,117 --> 00:10:01,317
I'm not giving up!

175
00:10:01,317 --> 00:10:04,617
I won't let them take the Mary away from me!

176
00:10:05,457 --> 00:10:06,497
This is stupid!

177
00:10:07,437 --> 00:10:10,857
You got fooled by a bunch of salesmen trying to pawn off a used boat!

178
00:10:11,477 --> 00:10:14,837
Luffy I know wouldn't cave in to some sales bitch from a total stranger!

179
00:10:15,377 --> 00:10:19,177
He'd believe in the strength of the Mary and the strength of his crew!

180
00:10:19,177 --> 00:10:22,817
But here you are, acting like you know everything and ignoring your friends!

181
00:10:23,437 --> 00:10:26,357
I can't believe that's the kind of captain you turned out to be!

182
00:10:26,537 --> 00:10:28,157
I thought you were better than that!

183
00:10:28,817 --> 00:10:30,537
You're not being fair, Usopp!

184
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:31,337
Luffy felt that...

185
00:10:31,337 --> 00:10:32,497
You stay out of this!

186
00:10:32,637 --> 00:10:34,477
It was my call, I stand by it!

187
00:10:34,757 --> 00:10:36,137
There's nothing you can do!

188
00:10:36,497 --> 00:10:38,957
We're getting a new ship, whether you like it or not!

189
00:10:39,257 --> 00:10:41,037
This is the end of the road for the Mary!

190
00:10:41,177 --> 00:10:42,297
I'm not leaving her here!

191
00:10:42,337 --> 00:10:43,597
I don't care what you say!

192
00:10:43,597 --> 00:10:48,257
I know you're always trying to think about the future, but not every one of this crew is like that!

193
00:10:48,497 --> 00:10:50,577
I see the Mary as one of our friends, got it?

194
00:10:50,617 --> 00:10:52,697
And I won't abandon her when she's hers!

195
00:10:52,797 --> 00:10:53,717
Don't be stupid!

196
00:10:53,997 --> 00:10:56,417
Even if she is a friend, that doesn't mean she's a person!

197
00:10:56,537 --> 00:10:59,057
She is to me, and she still has the strength to live!

198
00:10:59,177 --> 00:11:03,117
But you wouldn't appreciate that, because all you care about is getting a new ship to play with!

199
00:11:03,137 --> 00:11:03,737
Alright, that's enough!

200
00:11:03,897 --> 00:11:06,277
Stop being so selfish and think about your crew!

201
00:11:06,437 --> 00:11:07,717
Dude, listen to yourself!

202
00:11:08,197 --> 00:11:11,257
Luffy, don't act like you're the only one who's torn up about this!

203
00:11:11,317 --> 00:11:12,697
We all feel the same way!

204
00:11:12,697 --> 00:11:15,497
If that was true, then you wouldn't be looking for a new ship!

205
00:11:15,517 --> 00:11:16,257
Alright, fine!

206
00:11:16,397 --> 00:11:19,977
If you don't like the way your captain does things, then why don't you go ahead and get on-

207
00:11:19,977 --> 00:11:24,937
Sanji!

208
00:11:30,937 --> 00:11:32,837
This is going way too far!

209
00:11:33,617 --> 00:11:35,317
What the hell is wrong with you?

210
00:11:35,957 --> 00:11:39,917
If you don't watch it, you're going to say something you can't take back, so calm down!

211
00:11:42,697 --> 00:11:51,517
Yeah, I'm sorry.

212
00:11:52,137 --> 00:11:53,537
I don't know what I was thinking.

213
00:11:53,957 --> 00:11:58,037
You don't have to apologize, because that's how you really feel, isn't it?

214
00:11:58,277 --> 00:11:59,397
That's not true!

215
00:11:59,397 --> 00:12:06,197
Just get rid of your dead weight and move on before they can slow you down!

216
00:12:07,717 --> 00:12:12,477
If you're going to throw away the Mary, might as well throw me away too!

217
00:12:12,477 --> 00:12:33,917
Just get rid of your dead weight and move on before they can slow you down!

218
00:12:33,917 --> 00:12:40,317
If you're going to throw away the Mary, might as well throw me away too!

219
00:12:41,137 --> 00:12:44,457
I know you're pissed off, but don't say stupid crap like that!

220
00:12:44,457 --> 00:12:46,057
No, I'm serious.

221
00:12:46,537 --> 00:12:48,377
I've been thinking about this for a while now.

222
00:12:50,057 --> 00:12:51,657
It isn't like it was before.

223
00:12:52,297 --> 00:12:53,877
You guys are just too strong for me.

224
00:12:54,397 --> 00:12:55,677
I can't keep up anymore.

225
00:12:56,617 --> 00:12:58,517
I mean, look what happened today.

226
00:12:58,817 --> 00:13:00,617
You can't even trust me with your money.

227
00:13:02,037 --> 00:13:05,777
There's no point in keeping me around if all I do is cause you trouble.

228
00:13:05,777 --> 00:13:13,317
You don't want weak people on your crew, do you?

229
00:13:14,277 --> 00:13:18,477
Luffy, I still believe that you'll be king of the pirates one day.

230
00:13:19,277 --> 00:13:23,337
But as for me, I'm just lucky I was able to make it this far.

231
00:13:24,477 --> 00:13:27,437
Even back when we first met and I was going to set off alone,

232
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:31,077
you probably just invited me on your ship out of pity.

233
00:13:31,677 --> 00:13:32,997
What are you talking about?

234
00:13:33,577 --> 00:13:34,357
Get on already.

235
00:13:34,357 --> 00:13:36,517
We're friends, right? So get on.

236
00:13:40,797 --> 00:13:42,517
That's the only reason I'm here.

237
00:13:44,917 --> 00:13:48,437
There's no sense traveling together if we don't even have the same goal.

238
00:13:50,977 --> 00:13:52,977
Hey, Usopp, where are you going?

239
00:13:54,277 --> 00:13:56,977
Wherever I go, it's my business.

240
00:13:57,397 --> 00:13:59,257
It has nothing to do with you anymore.

241
00:14:01,437 --> 00:14:02,377
Sorry, guys.

242
00:14:04,357 --> 00:14:07,137
I'm leaving the crew.

243
00:14:07,817 --> 00:14:08,737
This is goodbye.

244
00:14:08,737 --> 00:14:08,797
Goodbye.

245
00:14:08,797 --> 00:14:12,677
Usopp, why?

246
00:14:16,677 --> 00:14:17,237
Oh, no.

247
00:14:17,237 --> 00:14:28,797
Usopp, why?

248
00:14:28,797 --> 00:14:30,277
Oh, no.

249
00:14:30,277 --> 00:14:34,497
Hey, don't just sit there, Luffy.

250
00:14:34,997 --> 00:14:37,077
Who knows what he's going to do out there.

251
00:14:37,077 --> 00:14:39,137
Go say something to him.

252
00:14:39,137 --> 00:14:41,277
Stop him before it's too late.

253
00:14:45,157 --> 00:14:47,017
We've come too far together.

254
00:14:47,377 --> 00:14:49,437
We can't part ways like this.

255
00:14:49,957 --> 00:14:51,437
Usopp's not just a crew member.

256
00:14:52,017 --> 00:14:54,017
He's one of our friends too, isn't he?

257
00:14:55,177 --> 00:14:57,057
Get off and stop him!

258
00:14:57,057 --> 00:15:00,437
Luffy, what's wrong?

259
00:15:00,437 --> 00:15:03,797
Please, you're the captain, aren't you?

260
00:15:08,517 --> 00:15:09,077
Fine.

261
00:15:09,437 --> 00:15:10,877
Have it your way then.

262
00:15:10,877 --> 00:15:15,257
Uthopp!

263
00:15:15,257 --> 00:15:17,997
Get back here!

264
00:15:18,257 --> 00:15:19,677
It shouldn't be like this!

265
00:15:19,937 --> 00:15:21,657
Come on, we can talk!

266
00:15:21,737 --> 00:15:23,217
Yeah, come back!

267
00:15:23,337 --> 00:15:24,917
I want you to stay!

268
00:15:25,297 --> 00:15:26,737
Don't leave us!

269
00:15:29,337 --> 00:15:31,077
Uthopp, please!

270
00:15:32,337 --> 00:15:33,817
Say something.

271
00:15:33,817 --> 00:16:01,577
Luffy, I'm sorry I can't follow you anymore.

272
00:16:01,577 --> 00:16:05,897
And I'm sorry I was a pain till the bitter end.

273
00:16:08,457 --> 00:16:12,137
I know you're the captain of this ship, so the Mary belongs to you.

274
00:16:14,677 --> 00:16:17,777
That's why I want you to fight me, Monkey D. Luffy.

275
00:16:26,237 --> 00:16:28,317
I challenge you to a duel!

276
00:16:31,577 --> 00:16:38,977
Whoa, wait, what are you saying?

277
00:16:41,037 --> 00:16:43,917
At 10 o'clock tonight, I'll be back.

278
00:16:44,137 --> 00:16:46,157
So you better be ready for a fight, Captain.

279
00:16:46,777 --> 00:16:49,077
I can't stop you from destroying your own ship.

280
00:16:49,257 --> 00:16:51,797
But if I win, I'm taking the Mary and leaving.

281
00:16:52,837 --> 00:16:56,677
Either way, when we're done, the last bond between us will be broken.

282
00:16:56,677 --> 00:17:06,797
What's with you?

283
00:17:06,957 --> 00:17:08,697
Would you stop this nonsense already?

284
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:13,457
Usopp just got worked up because things were moving too fast, right?

285
00:17:13,677 --> 00:17:17,057
That's no reason to fight with your own friend, especially when he's hurt.

286
00:17:17,437 --> 00:17:21,097
If you give it some time, I'm sure both of you will see how silly this is.

287
00:17:21,097 --> 00:17:24,277
You've gone too far to turn back now.

288
00:17:24,757 --> 00:17:25,817
That's not true.

289
00:17:26,057 --> 00:17:29,837
There's nothing stopping you from apologizing and talking it over one more time.

290
00:17:29,837 --> 00:17:39,017
Like I said, no turning back.

291
00:17:39,797 --> 00:17:40,997
And why not?

292
00:17:41,877 --> 00:17:44,437
Usopp is willing to risk his life to fight me.

293
00:17:44,717 --> 00:17:46,157
He's more than just angry.

294
00:17:46,837 --> 00:17:50,077
Besides, if just talking it over was enough to make things right,

295
00:17:50,237 --> 00:17:52,477
we wouldn't have come to this in the first place.

296
00:17:53,397 --> 00:17:55,377
That's all I have to say, so goodnight.

297
00:17:57,637 --> 00:17:58,037
Luffy.

298
00:17:59,297 --> 00:18:00,217
Think about it.

299
00:18:00,557 --> 00:18:03,397
You said the Frankie family came here this afternoon, right?

300
00:18:03,797 --> 00:18:04,137
Yeah.

301
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:05,997
So, what are you trying to say?

302
00:18:06,197 --> 00:18:07,817
If you hadn't let them off so easy,

303
00:18:07,897 --> 00:18:10,297
they wouldn't have stolen the money from us in the first place.

304
00:18:10,397 --> 00:18:12,377
It's your fault those guys attacked Usopp.

305
00:18:12,477 --> 00:18:14,297
He's just freaking out because he feels guilty.

306
00:18:14,697 --> 00:18:17,777
Hey, don't go blaming me for not kicking their asses hard enough.

307
00:18:17,877 --> 00:18:19,777
You were the one who ran off to go shopping.

308
00:18:19,777 --> 00:18:22,197
What am I supposed to cook if I don't have any food?

309
00:18:22,197 --> 00:18:23,337
Both of you, shut up!

310
00:18:24,557 --> 00:18:26,397
There's been enough fighting already.

311
00:18:28,777 --> 00:18:30,697
Whatever happened, it's over now.

312
00:18:30,837 --> 00:18:31,557
Oh, I know.

313
00:18:31,837 --> 00:18:34,137
But this wouldn't be happening if it wasn't for him.

314
00:18:37,757 --> 00:18:38,557
Oh, hey.

315
00:18:38,997 --> 00:18:39,617
You're back.

316
00:18:40,177 --> 00:18:42,037
You were going after Usopp, weren't you?

317
00:18:44,777 --> 00:18:47,557
Even if he was mad, I still wanted to treat his wounds.

318
00:18:48,077 --> 00:18:49,217
But he turned me away.

319
00:18:50,217 --> 00:18:51,777
He found a place to stay.

320
00:18:52,197 --> 00:18:53,817
So, at least he can get some rest.

321
00:18:54,517 --> 00:18:56,097
But do you know what he said to me?

322
00:18:56,817 --> 00:18:58,497
He said we aren't friends now.

323
00:18:59,157 --> 00:19:02,677
So, I should leave him alone and go back to the ship.

324
00:19:02,677 --> 00:19:09,397
Just this morning, we were all so happy.

325
00:19:09,397 --> 00:19:10,457
And now what?

326
00:19:14,077 --> 00:19:15,597
We lost Usopp.

327
00:19:16,277 --> 00:19:17,477
Robin's still missing.

328
00:19:18,137 --> 00:19:20,417
I feel like if we don't do something,

329
00:19:21,197 --> 00:19:23,717
the whole crew is going to fall apart.

330
00:19:23,717 --> 00:19:35,717
Well, the straw hats, huh?

331
00:19:37,717 --> 00:19:40,117
I have a bad feeling about tonight.

332
00:19:40,597 --> 00:19:42,537
I wonder what it is.

333
00:19:42,537 --> 00:19:45,617
It's ten o'clock.

334
00:19:46,257 --> 00:19:48,157
Usopp will be here any second now.

335
00:19:58,157 --> 00:19:58,757
Listen up.

336
00:19:59,057 --> 00:20:00,897
I don't want any of you leaving the ship.

337
00:20:01,377 --> 00:20:02,137
You got that?

338
00:20:02,137 --> 00:20:09,677
Look.

339
00:20:09,957 --> 00:20:11,137
Please don't fight!

340
00:20:11,137 --> 00:20:12,137
Wait!

341
00:20:41,137 --> 00:21:11,117
ORCHESTRA PLAYS

342
00:21:11,137 --> 00:21:16,497
So you didn't lose your nerve after all.

343
00:21:16,957 --> 00:21:19,517
No matter how this battle ends, you can't regret it.

344
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:21,637
This is exactly what you asked for.

345
00:21:22,117 --> 00:21:22,957
That's perfect.

346
00:21:23,517 --> 00:21:24,777
Don't go easy on me.

347
00:21:25,337 --> 00:21:27,117
I won't be the underdog this time.

348
00:21:27,397 --> 00:21:30,697
In fact, I've already figured out a way to defeat you.

349
00:21:41,137 --> 00:21:55,457
I won't be the underdog this time.

350
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:11,898
On the next One Piece Luffy vs Usopp collision of two men's prides

351
00:23:12,158 --> 00:23:14,158
I'm gonna be king of the pirates

